{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Multi-tasking, Multi-processor and Distributed OS"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about different types of Operating Systems."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the application instalation program, using IT development tools available in the market, based on solution architecture features.  Understands the concepts of server, its characteristics and its relation with operating systems."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the operating systems, server operating systems and relevant information related with the user manual."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verbs for Speculating- Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs of speculation</span> to make guesses about the future or the present. They help you express the degrees of certainty in a sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs of speculation</span> show the probability of a situation from the speaker's perspective. In this order of ideas,  the speaker might be either wrong or right about what he/she is speculating."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs used to speculate</span> depend on how certain the speaker is regarding the sentence uttered. Take a look at the following modal verbs: </br></br><span class=\"strong\">MUST</br>MAY</br>COULD</br>CAN'T</br>MIGHT</br>WOULD</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You need to remember modal verbs never take \u201c<span class=\"italic\">s</span>\u201d in the third person of the singular <span class=\"italic\">He/She/It.</span> Likewise, the main verb after these <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> never come with the preposition <span class=\"strong\">to</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the case of \"would\",  it expresses what you think will happen. <br /> Example: <br /> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Using a multi- tasking operating system would give the impression that everyone is sharing one computer at the same time.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Using multitasking OS would give users the perception of having their own computer."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The symmetric OS would use an identical copy of the OS and share the memory."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Multi-tasking, Multi-processor and Distributed Operating Systems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Multi-tasking, Multi-processor and Distributed are types of Operating Systems with some differences and similarities."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">Multi-tasking Operating Systems</span> are an extension of multiprogramming systems. It allows many users from different locations to use a computer at the same time. It gives users the illusion of having their own machine, and allows duplication of software."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">Multi-processor systems</span> have more than one process in close communication. They share the same computer bus, memory, and the clock. These types of systems may also share peripheral devices to increase reliability."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've read multiprocessor systems may share the same bus and sometimes peripheral devices."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They distribute the computation among many physical processors. All processors have a separate memory and communicate through buses."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "file sharing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "distribution of files among different users"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One of the benefits of this type of OS is that it provides file sharing and runs independently from other computers on the network. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "host "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to receive or serve as a host"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These OS use their CPU for many jobs; it gives the possibility of hosting many users."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "job"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in OS, it is a unit of work given to the Operating System "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These OS use their CPU for many jobs; it gives the possibility of hosting many users."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "master processor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a drive configured to give the commands and act as the main control "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The asymmetric OS would assign each processor a specific task, scheduling master, and slave processors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "peripheral"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "related to the devices such as keyboard, mouse or printers connected to a computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've read multiprocessor systems may share the same bus and sometimes peripheral devices."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slave processor "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a drive configured to be controlled by another device"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The asymmetric OS would assign each processor a specific task, scheduling master and slave processors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le02ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about multi-tasking operating systems, multi-processor operating systems and distributed operating systems"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Focus on the benefits each one the systems provide. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Organize the most important information in a Venn diagram. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give an oral presentation to explain to your partners the benefits of each one of the systems. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about multi-tasking, multi-processor and distributed operating systems. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find information about the benefits each one of the systems provide. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I organize the information in a Venn diagram."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners the benefits each system offers. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Instructor:</span> Today, as part of the course we've been studying, we are going to discuss the main characteristics of multi-tasking, multi-processor, and distributed operating systems. Jay, please explain to us multi-tasking OS. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Jay:</span> Sure, Multitasking Operating Systems are an extension of multiprogramming systems. These OS use their CPU for many jobs; it gives the possibility of hosting many users. Using multitasking OS would give users the perception of having their own computer. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Instructor:</span> What have you found out about multiprocessor systems?"}, {"time": "40700", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jay:</span> I've read multiprocessor systems may share the same bus and sometimes peripheral devices. There are two main types: the symmetric and asymmetric OS. The symmetric OS would use an identical copy of the OS and share the memory. The asymmetric OS would assign each processor a specific task, scheduling master, and slave processors; it is more used among large systems.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Instructor:</span>  What about distributed operating systems?<br />"}, {"time": "73000", "image": "enpe8n6le02ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jay:</span>They distribute the computation among many physical processors. All processors have a separate memory and communicate through buses, which make them have high speed systems. One of the benefits of this type of OS is that it provides file sharing and runs independently from other computers on the network. <br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Instructor:</span> That's correct. You've talked appropriately about the OS studied in the class. They're all designed with different purposes and work with different ways. Next class we'll continue with some other types of OS. It would give us a wider perspective in the software industry."}], "coverimg": "